              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Spanish for the tray, then the Spanish for the stopover."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: despegar",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "despegar — \"to take off; to unstick\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "El avión despega a las seis. The plane takes off at six."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The noun is el despegue, take-off."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "despegar is built on pegar \"to stick\" with des- \"un-\"; pegar is inherited from Latin picāre \"to smear with pitch\" (EtymDB). A plane unsticks itself from the ground."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
